  ('8d3ac3b5-2086-42b9-a5c0-8285ea07106b', 'Tangzu Wan''er', 'tangzu-wan-er', '<div style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif; color:#222; line-height:1.8; max-width:1000px; margin:auto;">

  <!-- Header -->
  <div style="text-align:center; padding:30px; background:#f5f5f7; border-radius:15px;">
    <h1 style="font-size:34px; margin-bottom:10px;">Tangzu Wan’er</h1>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#555;">
      Budget Hi-Fi In-Ear Monitor with Warm Neutral Sound & Natural Vocal Tuning
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Product Description -->
  <div style="padding:25px 10px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:26px;">Product Description</h2>

    <p>
      The Tangzu Wan’er is one of the most popular entry-level Hi-Fi in-ear monitors, known for its natural tonality, smooth tuning, and exceptional value for money.
      It is designed for users who want a pleasant and non-fatiguing listening experience for daily use.
    </p>

    <p>
      It features a single 10mm dynamic driver that delivers a warm-neutral sound signature with slightly boosted mid-bass for added fullness.
      Vocals sound natural and engaging, making it especially good for songs, podcasts, and casual gaming.
    </p>

    <p>
      The tuning is carefully balanced to avoid harshness, making it comfortable for long listening sessions without ear fatigue.
      While it is not heavily bass-focused, it provides enough low-end presence for an enjoyable and relaxed sound profile.
    </p>

    <p>
      The lightweight resin shell and ergonomic shape ensure excellent comfort and fit.
      With a detachable 2-pin cable design, the Wan’er also offers durability and upgrade flexibility.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Key Features -->
  <div style="padding:10px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:26px;">Key Features</h2>

    <ul style="padding-left:20px; color:#444;">
      <li>10mm Dynamic Driver with Natural Tuning</li>
      <li>Warm-Neutral Sound Signature</li>
      <li>Clear and Natural Vocal Reproduction</li>
      <li>Soft Bass with Smooth Treble</li>
      <li>Detachable 2-Pin Cable System</li>
      <li>Ultra Comfortable Lightweight Design</li>
      <li>Good Passive Noise Isolation</li>
      <li>Ideal for Beginners & Daily Listening</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- Specification Table -->
  <div style="margin-top:20px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:26px;">Specifications</h2>

    <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:15px;">
      <tr style="background:#111; color:#fff;">
        <th style="padding:12px; text-align:left;">Feature</th>
        <th style="padding:12px; text-align:left;">Details</th>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Model</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Tangzu Wan’er</td>
      </tr>

      <tr style="background:#f9f9f9;">
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Driver Type</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">10mm Dynamic Driver</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Sound Signature</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Warm-Neutral</td>
      </tr>

      <tr style="background:#f9f9f9;">
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Frequency Range</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">20Hz – 20kHz</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Impedance</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">~20Ω</td>
      </tr>

      <tr style="background:#f9f9f9;">
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Sensitivity</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">~107 dB</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Cable Type</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Detachable 2-Pin (0.78mm)</td>
      </tr>

      <tr style="background:#f9f9f9;">
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Cable Material</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">OFC (Oxygen-Free Copper)</td>
      </tr>

