  ('1215d60d-6cdb-47ea-a6b2-a7310919bda8', 'Arduino Uno R3 SMD', 'arduino-uno-r3-smd-mufnuzxw', '<div class="product-description">

  <h2>Arduino Uno R3 SMD CH340G Development Board</h2>

  <p>
    The <strong>Arduino Uno R3 SMD CH340G</strong> is an affordable development
    board based on the <strong>ATmega328 SMD microcontroller</strong>. It uses
    the <strong>CH340G USB-to-UART interface</strong> for USB connectivity and
    programming, making it suitable for electronics development, robotics,
    STEM education, automation, sensor projects, and embedded prototyping.
  </p>

  <p>
    Unlike the traditional DIP version, this board uses a
    <strong>Surface-Mount Device (SMD)</strong> version of the ATmega328.
    It provides the familiar Arduino Uno pin configuration with
    <strong>14 digital I/O pins</strong>, including <strong>6 PWM outputs</strong>,
    and <strong>6 analog input pins</strong>.
  </p>

  <p>
    The board operates at <strong>5V</strong> and has a recommended external
    input voltage of <strong>7V to 12V</strong>. It can be powered through
    either the <strong>DC power jack or USB</strong>.
  </p>


