  <h2>Key Features</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>ATmega328 SMD microcontroller</li>
    <li>CH340G USB-to-UART interface</li>
    <li>14 digital input/output pins</li>
    <li>6 PWM output pins</li>
    <li>6 analog input pins</li>
    <li>16 MHz clock speed</li>
    <li>32 KB Flash memory</li>
    <li>2 KB SRAM and 1 KB EEPROM</li>
    <li>On-board Power, Pin 13, RX and TX LEDs</li>
    <li>USB and DC Jack power options</li>
    <li>Compact SMD-based design</li>
  </ul>


  <h2>Power</h2>

  <p>
    The Arduino Uno R3 SMD can be powered through the USB connection or
    external DC power jack. The recommended input voltage is
    <strong>7V to 12V</strong>.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Operating Voltage:</strong> 5V</li>
    <li><strong>Recommended Input:</strong> 7V - 12V</li>
    <li><strong>Input Voltage Limit:</strong> 6V - 20V</li>
    <li><strong>Power Options:</strong> DC Jack or USB</li>
    <li><strong>3.3V Pin Current:</strong> 50 mA</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Avoid unnecessarily high input voltage through the barrel jack, as higher
    voltage increases heat dissipation in the onboard regulator.
  </p>


  <h2>Memory</h2>

  <p>
    The ATmega328 provides sufficient memory for Arduino-based electronics,
    robotics, automation, and embedded projects.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Flash Memory:</strong> 32 KB</li>
    <li><strong>Bootloader:</strong> 0.5 KB</li>
    <li><strong>SRAM:</strong> 2 KB</li>
    <li><strong>EEPROM:</strong> 1 KB</li>
  </ul>


  <h2>Input and Output</h2>

  <p>
    The board provides 14 digital I/O pins and 6 analog inputs for connecting
    sensors, LEDs, displays, switches, motors, modules, and other electronic
    components.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Digital I/O:</strong> 14 pins</li>
    <li><strong>PWM:</strong> 6 pins</li>
    <li><strong>Analog Inputs:</strong> 6 pins</li>
    <li><strong>Maximum I/O Current:</strong> 40 mA per pin</li>
  </ul>


  <h2>USB Interface & Programming</h2>

  <p>
    This version uses the <strong>CH340G USB-to-UART converter</strong>
    instead of the ATmega16U2 interface used on the standard Arduino Uno R3.
    It provides USB connectivity for programming and serial communication.
  </p>

  <p>
    Depending on the operating system, a compatible <strong>CH340/CH341
    driver</strong> may be required so that the board can be detected as a
    virtual COM port.
  </p>


  <h2>Applications</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Academic robotics and STEM projects</li>
    <li>Sensor grid prototyping</li>
    <li>Embedded automation projects</li>
    <li>Data logging using SPI or I2C peripherals</li>
    <li>Smart home relay control prototypes</li>
    <li>Motor speed regulation</li>
    <li>Actuator management</li>
    <li>Signal processing and prototyping</li>
    <li>General electronics development</li>
  </ul>


  <h2>Important Notes</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>
      A compatible CH340 serial driver may be required for proper USB
      communication with the computer.
    </li>

    <li>
      Do not exceed the maximum <strong>40 mA</strong> current rating of an
      individual I/O pin.
    </li>

    <li>
      Higher input voltage through the barrel jack can increase heat
      dissipation in the onboard voltage regulator.
    </li>

    <li>
      The ATmega328 SMD controller is permanently mounted on the PCB and is
      not removable like a traditional DIP package.
    </li>
  </ul>


  <h2>Package Includes</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>1 × Arduino Uno R3 SMD CH340G Development Board</li>
    <li>1 × USB Interface / Programming Cable</li>
