  ('2e19adc1-177e-4a2e-ad39-f83555a26006', 'Plextone G25', 'plextone-g25', '<div style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif; color:#222; line-height:1.8; max-width:1000px; margin:auto;">

  <!-- Header -->
  <div style="text-align:center; padding:30px; background:#f5f5f7; border-radius:15px;">
    <h1 style="font-size:34px; margin-bottom:10px;">Plextone G25</h1>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:#555;">
      Gaming In-Ear Earphones with Deep Bass, Noise Isolation & Clear Mic Performance
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Product Description -->
  <div style="padding:25px 10px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:26px;">Product Description</h2>

    <p>
      The Plextone G25 is a budget gaming earphone designed for mobile and PC gamers who need clear directional sound and strong bass performance.
      It features a 10mm dynamic driver that enhances low-frequency sounds, making footsteps, gunshots, and in-game effects more noticeable.
    </p>

    <p>
      With its gaming-optimized tuning, the G25 improves sound positioning, helping players detect enemy movements more accurately in FPS games.
      The anti-interference microphone ensures clearer voice communication during team gameplay or calls.
    </p>

    <p>
      The earphones come with a magnetic design that allows easy storage when not in use and a comfortable memory foam ear tip for noise isolation.
      The long cable design (around 1.6m–2.2m depending on setup) supports both mobile and desktop gaming setups.
    </p>

    <p>
      Overall, Plextone G25 is built for gamers who want affordable but powerful wired earphones with strong bass and reliable voice clarity.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Key Features -->
  <div style="padding:10px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:26px;">Key Features</h2>

    <ul style="padding-left:20px; color:#444;">
      <li>10mm Dynamic Driver with Enhanced Bass</li>
      <li>Gaming Optimized Sound for FPS Awareness</li>
      <li>Anti-Interference Built-in Microphone</li>
      <li>Magnetic Earbud Design</li>
      <li>Memory Foam Ear Tips for Noise Isolation</li>
      <li>Long Cable for Mobile & PC Use</li>
      <li>Clear Voice Communication</li>
      <li>Comfortable for Long Gaming Sessions</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- Specification Table -->
  <div style="margin-top:20px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:26px;">Specifications</h2>

    <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:15px;">
      <tr style="background:#111; color:#fff;">
        <th style="padding:12px; text-align:left;">Feature</th>
        <th style="padding:12px; text-align:left;">Details</th>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Model</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Plextone G25</td>
      </tr>

      <tr style="background:#f9f9f9;">
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Product Type</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Wired Gaming Earphones</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Driver Size</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">10mm Dynamic Driver</td>
      </tr>

      <tr style="background:#f9f9f9;">
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Frequency Range</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">20Hz – 20kHz</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Sensitivity</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">~102–108dB</td>
      </tr>

      <tr style="background:#f9f9f9;">
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Impedance</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">16Ω</td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Cable Length</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Approx. 1.6m – 2.2m (with extension)</td>
      </tr>

      <tr style="background:#f9f9f9;">
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">Connector</td>
        <td style="padding:10px; border:1px solid #ddd;">3.5mm Jack</td>
